<strong>Very small kitchen ideas on a budget</strong> don't have to involve a complete renovation. With a few clever design decisions, you can make a compact kitchen feel brighter, more organised and surprisingly spacious without stretching your budget. Whether you're updating a rental, renovating your first home or refreshing an older kitchen, these practical ideas can help you achieve a stylish result for less.
<h3>1. Paint the Cabinets Instead of Replacing Them</h3>
New cabinetry can be expensive, but repainting existing cabinets is one of the most cost-effective ways to transform a small kitchen.

Soft whites, warm greys and muted sage greens help reflect light and create a fresh, modern appearance without the cost of a full replacement. Exploring tailored <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/kitchen-cabinet-design/">clever kitchen cabinet design</a> ideas can inspire creative two-tone colour combinations.
<h3>2. Replace Handles for an Instant Upgrade</h3>
