Small details make a noticeable difference.

Swapping outdated cabinet handles for contemporary brass, matt black or brushed nickel options can instantly modernise your kitchen while costing a fraction of a renovation.

It's one of the easiest weekend projects with impressive results.
<h3>3. Add Open Shelving to Create More Space</h3>
Bulky wall units can make a tiny kitchen feel enclosed.

Replacing one or two upper cabinets with open shelving creates a lighter appearance while giving you somewhere to display attractive crockery, glassware or plants.

Just remember to avoid overcrowding the shelves, as too many items can have the opposite effect. For streamlined alternatives, consider layout efficiencies borrowed from modern <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/small-modular-kitchen-design/">small modular kitchen design solutions</a>.
<h3>4. Maximise Every Corner</h3>
Corners are often wasted in compact kitchens.

Simple corner shelves, pull-out organisers or rotating storage trays can make awkward spaces far more practical without major building work.

